1. Quick Architecture Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 3-tier mental model:\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 [User Speech / Avatars in Unity]\uc0\u8232           |\u8232    Audio Capture + VAD\u8232           v\u8232  [Realtime Session Manager]----> OpenAI 4o-mini Realtime Session (WebRTC / Websocket)\u8232           |                                 ^\u8232           | (text transcripts)              |\u8232           v                                 |\u8232    Query Classification  ---->  RAG Service (embedding search + metadata filters)\u8232           |                                 |\u8232       Retrieved Chunks  --------------------+ (injected into next model turn via system/content items)\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Key ideas:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Unity handles UX: microphone in, avatar expression out, partial streaming text/voice.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}A lightweight 
\f1\b RAG microservice
\f0\b0  handles offline doc ingestion + embeddings + vector search.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Before sending a user turn to the model, Unity (or a gateway) calls the RAG service, packages top-K snippets, and updates the 
\f1\b Realtime session instructions
\f0\b0  (conversation items) 
\f2\i just-in-time
\f0\i0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Maintain 
\f1\b memory layers
\f0\b0 : recent conversation state, user profile facts, and long-term semantic memory retrieved on demand.\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
