5. Context Assembly Strategy\
You have a token budget per model call. You need to merge:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}System persona / safety\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Instructions for using retrieved context\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Recent conversation turns (N-back)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}User profile memory
\f0\b0  (short bullet facts)\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Retrieved snippets
\f0\b0  (top-K, trimmed)\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 5.1 Token Budget Heuristic\
Let 
\f1\b B = total ctx tokens
\f0\b0 . Reserve slices:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}System + policies: 5\'9610%\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Conversation recent window: 30%\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Retrieved knowledge: 40%\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}User memory & persona: 10%\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Slack (buffer for model output & auto-expansion): 10\'9615%\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 5.2 Compact Snippet Formatting\
Wrap snippets in tagged blocks so the model can cite them:\
<knowledge id="treehouse_energy_01" source="Treehouse User Guide">\uc0\u8232 Energy in Treehouse recharges 1 unit every 15 min... Users can watch ads...\u8232 </knowledge>\
Bundle all snippets into a 
\f1\b hidden system item
\f0\b0  or a 
\f1\b tool message
\f0\b0  before the model responds.\
5.3 Dedup & Summarize\
If multiple chunks from same doc rank high, summarize them into a shorter synthetic bullet set before injecting to save tokens.\
